	// A nested group is a subinterval [i, j] ⊆ [start, end] where min(lcp[i..j]) > minL
	// These are groups with longer matching sequences

	// Actually, the approach is: for each pair (i, j) in SA where lcp[k] >= threshold for
	// all k in [i+1, j], they share a common prefix of length = min(lcp[i+1..j])
	// We want all maximal groups

	// The proper way to enumerate all clone groups is via the "enhanced suffix array" approach
	// or simply by finding all pairs and merging transitively

	// Let me use a simpler approach: find all intervals [l, r] in SA where
	// for all i in [l+1, r]: lcp[i] >= threshold
	// These are the maximal intervals. For nested intervals with higher min LCP,
	// those are handled by checking if they're subsumed.

